LOCATION:SRJC Petaluma Cafe Patio
SUMMARY:Sound of Our Stories - Open Mic
DESCRIPTION:Join us each month for the Sound of our Stories Campus Commun
 ity Luncheon. The monthly series will create a recurring\, student-led pe
 rformance space where participants are invited to center their cultural i
 dentities\, lived experiences\, and creative traditions through dance\, m
 usic\, spoken word\, poetry slam\, storytelling\, and other expressive ar
 t forms. Each event will be free and open to the SRJC community and hoste
 d on campus.  Students who perform will be given a $50 incentive.Sign up 
 to perform! (https://santarosajuniorcollege.formstack.com/forms/sounds_of
 _our_story)Sounds of Our Story website. (https://petaluma.santarosa.edu/s
 ounds-our-story)  This campus community event is funded by a grant from t
 he Santa Rosa Junior College Foundation Randolph Newman Cultural Enrichme
 nt Endowment.  All are welcome to attend!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join us each month for the Sound of our
  Stories Campus Community Luncheon. The monthly series will create a recu
 rring\, student-led performance space where participants are invited to c
 enter their cultural identities\, lived experiences\, and creative tradit
 ions through dance\, music\, spoken word\, poetry slam\, storytelling\, a
 nd other expressive art forms. Each event will be free and open to the SR
 JC community and hosted on campus.</p><p>  Students who perform will be g
 iven a $50 incentive.</p><p><a href="https://santarosajuniorcollege.forms
 tack.com/forms/sounds_of_our_story" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sign u
 p to perform!</a></p><p><a href="https://petaluma.santarosa.edu/sounds-ou
 r-story" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sounds of Our Story website.</a><
 /p><p>  This campus community event is funded by a grant from the Santa R
 osa Junior College Foundation Randolph Newman Cultural Enrichment Endowme
 nt.</p><p>  All are welcome to attend!</p>
