SUMMARY:AI With Purpose: Advancing Equity\, Belonging\, and Student Success
DESCRIPTION:Explore how California Community College practitioners are us
 ing artificial intelligence to strengthen support for undocumented and hi
 storically marginalized students. Panelists will share real-world example
 s of AI projects\, the challenges they sought to address\, and how equity
 \, trust\, privacy\, accessibility\, and human connection shaped their wo
 rk. Participants will leave with practical ideas and inspiration for thou
 ghtfully exploring how AI tools can support their own work and advance st
 udent success.  Viewing party at PAU Center - Bertolini 3rd Floor\, #4832
 Registration though Zoom. (https://foundationccc-org.zoom.us/webinar/regi
 ster/WN_1OBjC2fgTNyW09bxwo8biQ#/registration)For more information about U
 ndocumented Student Success Week\, visit the Undocu · Immigrant · Dream
  Center website.&#160\; (https://dream.santarosa.edu/workshops-events-202
 6-2027)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Explore how California Community Colleg
 e practitioners are using artificial intelligence to strengthen support f
 or undocumented and historically marginalized students. Panelists will sh
 are real-world examples of AI projects\, the challenges they sought to ad
 dress\, and how equity\, trust\, privacy\, accessibility\, and human conn
 ection shaped their work. Participants will leave with practical ideas an
 d inspiration for thoughtfully exploring how AI tools can support their o
 wn work and advance student success.</p><p>  Viewing party at PAU Center 
 - Bertolini 3rd Floor\, #4832</p><p><strong><a href="https://foundationcc
 c-org.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_1OBjC2fgTNyW09bxwo8biQ#/registration" t
 arget="_blank" rel="noopener">Registration though Zoom.</a></strong></p><
