X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T170000
LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Research Remix: Find Research Cite It Right with NoodleTools @ 4p
 m\, Oct 21st
DESCRIPTION:Join SRJC Librarian Canon Crawford and learn how to simplify 
 citations using the "NoodleTools" citation app. Along the way\, score qui
 ck tips on finding credible research in the library and on the Web.Noodle
 Tools helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliographies\, and offe
 rs note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features\, including the c
 apability to create papers via GoogleDocs.Workshop Details: Extra Credit 
 available!This NoodleTools workshop will use the MLA citation style\, whi
 ch is typically used in the English\, ESL\, Humanities\, Philosophy\, and
  Religion disciplines.If you are using APA\, take this workshop! We will 
 share how to choose this option in NoodleTools too.You will learn how to 
 sign up for an account with NoodleTools. We will provide examples to show
  how to create citations\, create a bibliography and check for errors.Alo
 ng the way\, you will receive quick tips on how to find credible research
  in the library and on the web.Check with your instructor to confirm the 
 citation style appropriate for your research assignment.Extra Credit: As 
 students\, you have the option to submit your instructor and course name 
 when you register if you would like us to notify your instructor that you
  have attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with your
  instructor on an alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.
 Registration: (click "Begin Registration" button below)This workshop requ
 ires registration in order to be admitted to the Zoom meeting.You will re
 ceive a confirmation email with the Zoom URL link for this workshop. Chec
 k your spam folder if you do not see it.This Zoom workshop will open 10 m
 inutes early to allow you time to log on.Attendees are asked to abide by 
 SRJC student conduct policy.Not familiar with Zoom? Watch this 1-minute v
 ideo on how to join a Zoom meeting.Have questions? Chat with an SRJC Libr
 arian!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Join SRJC Librarian Canon Crawford and learn
  how to simplify citations using the "NoodleTools" citation app. Along th
 e way\, score quick tips on finding credible research in the library and 
 on the Web.<br />NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA citations and bi
 bliographies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing fea
 tures\, including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs.<br />Wo
 rkshop Details: Extra Credit available!<br />This NoodleTools workshop wi
 ll use the MLA citation style\, which is typically used in the English\, 
 ESL\, Humanities\, Philosophy\, and Religion disciplines.<br />If you are
  using APA\, take this workshop! We will share how to choose this option 
 in NoodleTools too.<br />You will learn how to sign up for an account wit
 h NoodleTools. We will provide examples to show how to create citations\,
  create a bibliography and check for errors.<br />Along the way\, you wil
 l receive quick tips on how to find credible research in the library and 
 on the web.<br />Check with your instructor to confirm the citation style
  appropriate for your research assignment.<br />Extra Credit: As students
 \, you have the option to submit your instructor and course name when you
  register if you would like us to notify your instructor that you have at
 tended the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with your instruc
 tor on an alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.<br />Re
 gistration: (click "Begin Registration" button below)<br />This workshop 
 requires registration in order to be admitted to the Zoom meeting.<br />Y
 ou will receive a confirmation email with the Zoom URL link for this work
 shop. Check your spam folder if you do not see it.<br />This Zoom worksho
 p will open 10 minutes early to allow you time to log on.<br />Attendees 
 are asked to abide by SRJC student conduct policy.<br />Not familiar with
  Zoom? Watch this 1-minute video on how to join a Zoom meeting.<br />Have
  questions? Chat with an SRJC Librarian!
