DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T120000
LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Dave Kanter - Human Agency & Machine Inquiry
DESCRIPTION:As generative AI becomes embedded across disciplines\, higher
  education faces a pivotal moment—not of battle between opposing camps\
 , but of intentional design.  Generative systems offer novel capabilities
  for research\, creation\, and learning\, yet their ultimate value depend
 s entirely on how thoughtfully we guide them.Dave Kanter is an AI systems
  architect and engineering leader with provisional patent on agent feedba
 ck architecture.Learn more on the SRJC Computer Studies' AI Talks website
 . (https://cs.santarosa.edu/ai-talks-2026)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  As generative AI becomes embedded acros
 s disciplines\, higher education faces a pivotal moment—not of battle b
 etween opposing camps\, but of intentional design.</p><p>  Generative sys
 tems offer novel capabilities for research\, creation\, and learning\, ye
 t their ultimate value depends entirely on how thoughtfully we guide them
 .</p><p><strong>Dave Kanter</strong> is an AI systems architect and engin
 eering leader with provisional patent on agent feedback architecture.</p>
 <p><a href="https://cs.santarosa.edu/ai-talks-2026" target="_blank" rel="
 noopener">Learn more on the SRJC Computer Studies' AI Talks website.</a><
 /p>
