LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Navigating Research with AI Tools at SRJC Libraries @ 4pm\, Oct 2
 8th
DESCRIPTION:AI apps can empower researchers to discover topic connections
  and identify areas for further exploration. Librarian Canon Crawford wil
 l focus on responsible research practices and academic integrity while ex
 ploring AI tools at SRJC Libraries.Workshop Details: Extra Credit availab
 le!Extra Credit: As students\, you have the option to submit your instruc
 tor and course name when you register if your instructor is offering extr
 a credit and you would like us to notify your instructor that you have at
 tended. Or\, you can work with your instructor on an alternative way to p
 rovide evidence of your attendance.Registration: (click "Begin Registrati
 on" button below)This workshop requires registration in order to be admit
 ted to the Zoom meeting.You will receive a confirmation email with the Zo
 om URL link for this workshop. Check your spam folder if you do not see i
 t.This Zoom workshop will open 10 minutes early to allow you time to log 
 on.Attendees are asked to abide by SRJC student conduct policy.Not famili
 ar with Zoom? Watch this 1-minute video on how to join a Zoom meeting.Hav
 e questions? Chat with an SRJC Librarian!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:AI apps can empower researchers to discover 
 topic connections and identify areas for further exploration. Librarian C
 anon Crawford will focus on responsible research practices and academic i
 ntegrity while exploring AI tools at SRJC Libraries.<br />Workshop Detail
 s: Extra Credit available!<br />Extra Credit: As students\, you have the 
 option to submit your instructor and course name when you register if you
 r instructor is offering extra credit and you would like us to notify you
 r instructor that you have attended. Or\, you can work with your instruct
 or on an alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.<br />Reg
 istration: (click "Begin Registration" button below)<br />This workshop r
 equires registration in order to be admitted to the Zoom meeting.<br />Yo
 u will receive a confirmation email with the Zoom URL link for this works
 hop. Check your spam folder if you do not see it.<br />This Zoom workshop
  will open 10 minutes early to allow you time to log on.<br />Attendees a
 re asked to abide by SRJC student conduct policy.<br />Not familiar with 
 Zoom? Watch this 1-minute video on how to join a Zoom meeting.<br />Have 
 questions? Chat with an SRJC Librarian!
