BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T133000
LOCATION:Student Health Services\, Bertolini Student Center - Santa Rosa 
 Campus
SUMMARY:QPR (Question\, Persuade\, Refer)
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to recognize the warning signs of suicide\, start a
  supportive conversation\, and connect someone to help.  QPR (Question\, 
 Persuade\, Refer) is a suicide prevention training that gives you practic
 al skills to recognize when someone may be struggling and take action. Wh
 ether you're interested in mental health\, supporting friends and peers\,
  or simply want to be better prepared to help someone in need\, this trai
 ning can help you feel more confident responding to a crisis.  In this tr
 aining\, you'll learn how to:Recognize warning signs and risk factors  Id
 entify when someone may be experiencing a mental health crisis  Ask about
  suicide in a direct and supportive way  Connect someone with appropriate
  help and resources  Use the QPR approach to support someone in need  To 
 register visit the Student Health Services website. (https://shs.santaros
 a.edu/11-5-26-qpr)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Learn how to recognize the warning sign
 s of suicide\, start a supportive conversation\, and connect someone to h
 elp.</p><p>  QPR (Question\, Persuade\, Refer) is a suicide prevention tr
 aining that gives you practical skills to recognize when someone may be s
 truggling and take action. Whether you're interested in mental health\, s
 upporting friends and peers\, or simply want to be better prepared to hel
 p someone in need\, this training can help you feel more confident respon
 ding to a crisis.</p><p>  In this training\, you'll learn how to:</p><ul>
 <li>Recognize warning signs and risk factors  </li><li>Identify when some
 one may be experiencing a mental health crisis  </li><li>Ask about suicid
 e in a direct and supportive way  </li><li>Connect someone with appropria
 te help and resources  </li><li>Use the QPR approach to support someone i
 n need  </li></ul><p><a href="https://shs.santarosa.edu/11-5-26-qpr" targ
 et="_blank" rel="noopener">To register visit the Student Health Services 
 website.</a></p>
