BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261109T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261109T170000
LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Research Remix: Find Research Cite It Right with NoodleTools @ 4p
 m\, Nov 9th
DESCRIPTION:Join SRJC Librarian Jessica Harris and learn how to simplify 
 citations using the "NoodleTools" citation app. Along the way\, score qui
 ck tips on finding credible research in the library and on the Web.Noodle
 Tools helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliographies\, and offe
 rs note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features\, including the c
 apability to create papers via GoogleDocs.Workshop Details: Extra Credit 
 available!This NoodleTools workshop will use APA and/or MLA style as live
  demo examples\, depending on the participants that register.Don't worry!
  Jessica will share how to use both MLA and APA. You're covered!You will 
 learn how to sign up for an account with NoodleTools. We will provide exa
 mples to show how to create citations\, create a bibliography and check f
 or errors.Along the way\, you will receive quick tips on how to find cred
 ible research in the library and on the web.Check with your instructor to
  confirm the citation style appropriate for your research assignment.Extr
 a Credit: As students\, you have the option to submit your instructor and
  course name when you register if you would like us to notify your instru
 ctor that you have attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can w
 ork with your instructor on an alternative way to provide evidence of you
 r attendance.Registration: (click "Begin Registration" button below)This 
 workshop requires registration in order to be admitted to the Zoom meetin
 g.You will receive a confirmation email with the Zoom URL link for this w
 orkshop. Check your spam folder if you do not see it.This Zoom workshop w
 ill open 10 minutes early to allow you time to log on.Attendees are asked
  to abide by SRJC student conduct policy.Not familiar with Zoom? Watch th
 is 1-minute video on how to join a Zoom meeting.Have questions? Chat with
  an SRJC Librarian!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Join SRJC Librarian Jessica Harris and learn
  how to simplify citations using the "NoodleTools" citation app. Along th
 e way\, score quick tips on finding credible research in the library and 
 on the Web.<br />NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA citations and bi
 bliographies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing fea
 tures\, including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs.<br />Wo
 rkshop Details: Extra Credit available!<br />This NoodleTools workshop wi
 ll use APA and/or MLA style as live demo examples\, depending on the part
 icipants that register.<br />Don't worry! Jessica will share how to use b
 oth MLA and APA. You're covered!<br />You will learn how to sign up for a
 n account with NoodleTools. We will provide examples to show how to creat
 e citations\, create a bibliography and check for errors.<br />Along the 
 way\, you will receive quick tips on how to find credible research in the
  library and on the web.<br />Check with your instructor to confirm the c
 itation style appropriate for your research assignment.<br />Extra Credit
 : As students\, you have the option to submit your instructor and course 
 name when you register if you would like us to notify your instructor tha
 t you have attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with
  your instructor on an alternative way to provide evidence of your attend
 ance.<br />Registration: (click "Begin Registration" button below)<br />T
 his workshop requires registration in order to be admitted to the Zoom me
 eting.<br />You will receive a confirmation email with the Zoom URL link 
 for this workshop. Check your spam folder if you do not see it.<br />This
  Zoom workshop will open 10 minutes early to allow you time to log on.<br
  />Attendees are asked to abide by SRJC student conduct policy.<br />Not 
 familiar with Zoom? Watch this 1-minute video on how to join a Zoom meeti
 ng.<br />Have questions? Chat with an SRJC Librarian!
