BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261218
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261219
LOCATION:Multicultural Museum - Santa Rosa Campus
SUMMARY:Young\, Gifted\, and Black - Art Submissions Due
DESCRIPTION:Young\, Gifted\, and Black: Art by Black Students at SRJC is 
 an upcoming exhibition at the SRJC Multicultural Museum celebrating the c
 reativity and artistic voices of Black students across campus. Created in
  recognition of Black History Month\, the exhibition provides a dedicated
  space for Black student artists to have their work seen\, valued\, and c
 elebrated by the SRJC community.  Black students are invited to submit or
 iginal artwork in any medium or theme\, including visual art\, poetry\, a
 nd other forms of creative writing. Artwork does not need to focus on Bla
 ck identity or the Black experience—the exhibition celebrates the bread
 th of Black creativity and the individuality of each participating artist
 .  The exhibition will be on display in the ground floor library display 
 cases from the beginning of the Spring 2027 semester through Spring Break
 . Students interested in participating must drop off their work at the SR
 JC Multicultural Museum by December 18\, 2026.Learn more about the museum
  on the SRJC Multicultural Museum website. (https://museum.santarosa.edu/
 )
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><em>Young\, Gifted\, and Black: Art by Bl
 ack Students at SRJC</em> is an upcoming exhibition at the SRJC Multicult
 ural Museum celebrating the creativity and artistic voices of Black stude
 nts across campus. Created in recognition of Black History Month\, the ex
 hibition provides a dedicated space for Black student artists to have the
 ir work seen\, valued\, and celebrated by the SRJC community.</p><p>  Bla
 ck students are invited to submit original artwork in any medium or theme
 \, including visual art\, poetry\, and other forms of creative writing. A
 rtwork does not need to focus on Black identity or the Black experience�
 �the exhibition celebrates the breadth of Black creativity and the indivi
 duality of each participating artist.</p><p>  The exhibition will be on d
 isplay in the ground floor library display cases from the beginning of th
 e Spring 2027 semester through Spring Break. Students interested in parti
 cipating must drop off their work at the SRJC Multicultural Museum by Dec
 ember 18\, 2026.</p><p><a href="https://museum.santarosa.edu/" target="_b
 lank" rel="noopener">Learn more about the museum on the SRJC Multicultura
 l Museum website.</a></p>
UID:20261218T080000Z-24102@calendar.santarosa.edu
