X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270307
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270308
LOCATION:Multicultural Museum - Santa Rosa Campus
SUMMARY:Standing in Her Power: Portraits Beyond the Colonial Frame
DESCRIPTION:"Through portraiture\, we turn the camera toward dignity\, ag
 ency\, and self-representation. The women within these pages are dancers\
 , artists\, bead workers\, teachers\, mothers\, daughters\, grandmothers\
 , language keepers\, and land and water defenders. They are culture beare
 rs\, but they are not defined by what they carry for others." — Julian 
 Cook\, Co-Creator  A Portrait Series by Alexa LexMex Treviño (https://ww
 w.lexmexart.com/about) in collaboration with the SRJC Multicultural Museu
 m.This exhibit is funded by a grant from the Santa Rosa Junior College Fo
 undation Randolph Newman Cultural Enrichment Endowment.For more informati
 on\, visit the SRJC Multicultural Museum website. (https://museum.santaro
 sa.edu/event/standing-her-power-portraits-beyond-colonial-frame)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  "Through portraiture\, we turn the came
 ra toward dignity\, agency\, and self-representation. The women within th
 ese pages are dancers\, artists\, bead workers\, teachers\, mothers\, dau
 ghters\, grandmothers\, language keepers\, and land and water defenders. 
 They are culture bearers\, but they are not defined by what they carry fo
 r others." — Julian Cook\, Co-Creator</p><p>  A Portrait Series by <a h
 ref="https://www.lexmexart.com/about" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Alex
 a LexMex Treviño</a> in collaboration with the SRJC Multicultural Museum
 .</p><p><em>This exhibit is funded by a grant from the Santa Rosa Junior 
 College Foundation Randolph Newman Cultural Enrichment Endowment.</em></p
 ><p><a href="https://museum.santarosa.edu/event/standing-her-power-portra
 its-beyond-colonial-frame" target="_blank" rel="noopener">For more inform
 ation\, visit the SRJC Multicultural Museum website.</a></p>
